    "title": "NHL playoff picture, NHL schedule today, full standings, updated bracket",
    "text": "Updated April 14, 2026, 2:05 a.m. CTThe NHL playoff picture continues to form heading into the final week of the regular season.Nashville's 3-2 loss to San Jose on April 13 left the door open for the Los Angeles Kings to clinch the final playoff spot in the West and eliminate the Predators from contention.In the East, Philadelphia secured the third spot in the Metro with a shootout win over Carolina.Here's the full NHL playoff picture heading into tonight: NHL playoff pictureUpdating on April 13Western Conference standingsCentral Division top 31. Colorado Avalanche (117 points; clinched playoff berth, Central No. 1)Record: 53-16-11 | Regulation wins: 46 | Games remaining: 22. Dallas Stars (110 points; clinched playoff berth, Central No. 2)Record: 49-20-12 | Regulation wins: 38 | Games remaining: 13. Minnesota Wild (102 points; clinched playoff berth, Central No. 3)Record: 45-24-12 | Regulation wins: 30 | Games remaining: 1Pacific Division top 31. Vegas Golden Knights (93 points; clinched playoff berth)Record: 38-26-17 | Regulation wins: 29 | Games remaining: 22. Edmonton Oilers (91 points; clinched playoff berth)Record: 40-30-11 | Regulation wins: 31 | Games remaining: 23. Anaheim Ducks (90 points; clinched playoff berth)Record: 42-32-6 | Regulation wins: 25 | Games remaining: 2--------------------------Wild card standings1. Utah Mammoth (90 points; clinched playoff berth)Record: 42-32-6 | Regulation wins: 32 | Games remaining: 22. Los Angeles Kings (89 points)Record: 35-26-19 | Regulation wins: 22 | Games remaining: 2--------------------------3. Nashville Predators (86 points; eliminated from playoff contention)4. San Jose Sharks (84 points; eliminated from playoff contention)5. St. Louis Blues (82 points; eliminated from playoff contention)6. Winnipeg Jets (82 points; eliminated from playoff contention)7. Seattle Kraken (79 points; eliminated from playoff contention)8. Calgary Flames (75 points; eliminated from playoff contention)9. Chicago Blackhawks (70 points; eliminated from playoff contention)10. Vancouver Canucks (56 points; eliminated from playoff contention)--------------------------Eastern Conference standingsMetropolitan Division top 31. Carolina Hurricanes (111 points; clinched playoff berth, Metro No. 1)Record: 52-22-7 | Regulation wins: 38 | Games remaining: 12. Pittsburgh Penguins (98 points; clinched playoff berth, Metro No. 2)Record: 41-24-16 | Regulation wins: 34 | Games remaining: 13. Philadelphia Flyers (94 points; clinched playoff berth, Metro No. 3)Record: 41-27-12 | Regulation wins: 26 | Games remaining: 1Atlantic Division top 31. Buffalo Sabres (108 points; clinched playoff berth)Record: 50-23-8 | Regulation wins: 42 | Games remaining: 12. Tampa Bay Lightning (106 points; clinched playoff berth)Record: 50-25-6 | Regulation wins: 40 | Games remaining: 13. Montreal Canadiens (106 points; clinched playoff berth)Record: 48-23-10 | Regulation wins: 34 | Games remaining: 1--------------------------Wild card standings1. Boston Bruins (98 points; clinched playoff berth)Record: 44-27-10 | Regulation wins: 32 | Games remaining: 12. Ottawa Senators (97 points; clinched playoff berth)Record: 43-27-11 | Regulation wins: 37 | Games remaining: 1--------------------------3. Washington Capitals (93 points; eliminated from playoff contention)4. Detroit Red Wings (92 points; eliminated from playoff contention)5. Columbus Blue Jackets (92 points; eliminated from playoff contention)6. New York Islanders (91 points; eliminated from playoff contention)7. New Jersey Devils (87 points; eliminated from playoff contention)8. Florida Panthers (82 points; eliminated from playoff contention)9. Toronto Maple Leafs (78 points; eliminated from playoff contention)10. New York Rangers (75 points; eliminated from playoff contention) NHL playoffs projected first round matchupsUpdating on April 13Western ConferenceCentral No. 1 Colorado Avalanche vs. Wild card No. 2 Los Angeles KingsCentral No. 2 Dallas Stars vs. Central No. 3